WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.520
Part 2. You will hear a man giving a talk to people who are interested in starting their own

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:15.040
street food business. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.520
Good evening everyone, my name's John and I run VegOut, a street food business selling

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.759
vegan food. Since 2012, I've been travelling all around the country cooking vegan food

00:00:55.759 --> 00:01:01.840
in my converted van and selling it at all kinds of outdoor events. I'm here to give you some

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:09.199
advice based on my experience. The good news is that there's never been a better time to start

00:01:09.199 --> 00:01:17.120
your own street food business. Street food continues to grow in popularity. I think there

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:24.080
are a couple of reasons for this. The first is that street food is a reaction against fast food.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.639
Street food ranges from high quality burgers to vegan curries and everything in between.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:38.160
But while fast food is cheap and easy to find, it's not particularly good for you. It's also

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:43.519
the same everywhere. What you get with street food on the other hand is something different.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:50.720
People like the idea of trying something they can't get anywhere else. They also like seeing

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.879
food prepared in front of them and which hasn't come straight out of a freezer.

00:01:56.239 --> 00:02:01.760
You need to think about the best place to sell your street food. People always think music

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.760
festivals are an obvious place to start but the cost of renting a space can be huge and there's

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:15.199
always a lot of competition. Food markets on the other hand are great because customers are always

00:02:15.199 --> 00:02:20.960
really interested in food and give great feedback. And if you can get a spot in your

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.600
local park, fantastic. Usually very relaxed but with lots of customers passing by.

00:02:28.559 --> 00:02:33.839
Once you get established you'll start getting asked to do parties which can be really challenging

00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:39.039
but lots of fun. Having street food at weddings has become quite fashionable too

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.919
but you need to really know what you're doing as everything needs to be perfect.

00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:53.119
Before you hear the rest of the talk you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.119
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.199
Setting up a street food business costs a lot less than opening a restaurant or cafe

00:03:29.199 --> 00:03:35.520
but you'll have to buy some basic equipment. I try to get things like hobs and fridges second-hand

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.960
if you can but it's a lot of work and it's a lot of time and it's a lot of work and it's a lot of

00:03:41.279 --> 00:03:45.119
I try to get things like hobs and fridges second-hand if you can.

00:03:45.679 --> 00:03:49.279
You can replace them with better quality stuff if your business takes off.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.639
Renting is another option but you'll end up spending more money rather than saving it.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.639
You've probably got a good idea about the food you're planning to sell. I expect you've done

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:05.440
some research to find out if anyone else is selling a similar product and you'll have

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:11.759
thought about any possible allergies to nuts or eggs etc. But there's one thing people don't

00:04:11.759 --> 00:04:19.279
always think about and that's how you're going to serve it. On a plate? In a bag? Will you provide

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:26.559
a fork? Will it all be easily recyclable or reusable? It's got to be easy to eat and look

00:04:26.559 --> 00:04:33.600
attractive or customers won't come back. Once you get started you should be prepared for things to

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:40.880
go wrong. Every business faces problems and here are a few examples from street food businesses

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:48.480
that I know. My friends who run Thai Basil started by juggling their street food business

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.399
with their day jobs in a restaurant. Their work-life balance was non-existent as they were

00:04:54.399 --> 00:04:59.920
working till midnight in the restaurant all week and then took their food truck to markets on their

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:06.880
days off. The owners of Basque found it was hard to make a profit because the price of fish, essential

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.559
for some of their dishes, was so high and it was hard to charge customers a lot more for those

00:05:12.559 --> 00:05:20.640
dishes. So they had to stop focusing on fish dishes and include more vegetarian food. The owners of

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.000
Lou's Kitchen were making salads to order from their van and some of their dishes were quite

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.760
complicated. At one of their first events they ended up with people standing in a long queue for

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:38.959
more than 15 minutes and many of them lost patience. So make sure whatever you offer can be served

00:05:38.959 --> 00:05:47.040
quickly and efficiently. The owners of Chip Chop had found a perfect venue near a beach where there

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.200
weren't any other street food trucks but what they hadn't realised was that they'd need a special

00:05:53.200 --> 00:06:01.920
licence which individual businesses don't need at markets or festivals. It was a complicated process

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:08.959
and in the end they gave up. So I hope that's given you a flavour of some of the things that can happen.

00:06:12.559 --> 00:06:22.959
That is the end of part two. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part two.

